.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-SYSKLOGD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-sysklogd ,
.Nm klogd ,
.Nm logger ,
.Nm logread ,
.Nm syslogd
.Nd BusyBox log tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm klogd
.Op Fl c Ar N
.Op Fl n
.Nm logger
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl t Ar TAG
.Op Fl p Ar PRIO
.Op Ar MESSAGE
.Nm logread
.Op Fl fF
.Nm syslogd
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the sysklogd applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
The kernel's own log is
.Pa /dev/bootlog ;
see
.Xr bootlog 4 .
.Bl -tag -width syslogd
.It Nm klogd
Log kernel messages to syslog, which it reads with
.Xr syslog 2 .
.It Nm logger
Write
.Ar MESSAGE ,
or standard input, to syslog, through
.Pa /dev/log .
.It Nm logread
Display messages in the circular buffer of a
.Nm syslogd
started with
.Fl C ,
which keeps its messages in System V shared memory instead of a file.
.It Nm syslogd
Provide system logging.
.Pa /dev/log
is a link to
.Pa /var/run/log ,
where the daemon follows it and binds its Unix domain socket, as systemd's
link leads under
.Pa /run .
On the metal and GNU systems
.Xr init 8
keeps it running as
.Ql syslogd -n -O /var/log/messages -s 200 -b 1 :
the messages go to
.Pa /var/log/messages ,
which it moves to
.Pa /var/log/messages.0
past 200 KiB.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss klogd
.Bl -tag -width "-c N"
.It Fl c Ar N
Print messages more urgent than priority
.Ar N
to the console; without effect on Rach2, where the daemon does not run.
The priority is from 1 to 8.
.It Fl n
Run in the foreground.
.El
.Ss logger
.Bl -tag -width "-p PRIO"
.It Fl s
Log to standard error as well as the system log.
.It Fl t Ar TAG
Use the specified tag.
The default is the user name.
.It Fl p Ar PRIO
Set the priority as a number or a
.Ar FACILITY.LEVEL
pair.
.El
.Ss logread
.Bl -tag -width "-F"
.It Fl f
Output data as the log grows.
.It Fl F
Dump the buffer, then output data as the log grows.
.El
.Ss syslogd
.Bl -tag -width "-R HOST[:PORT]"
.It Fl n
Run in the foreground.
.It Fl R Ar HOST Ns Op : Ns Ar PORT
Log to the specified host and port.
The default port is 514.
.It Fl L
Log locally as well as over the network.
With
.Fl R ,
the default is to log only over the network.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/log/messages
.It Pa /dev/bootlog
Rach2 kernel log.
.It Pa /dev/log
The link to the system log's socket.
.It Pa /var/log/messages
The system log.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl logger "hello"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 2 ,
.Xr bootlog 4 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh HISTORY
The applet descriptions are adapted from BusyBox 1.36.1 usage text,
